  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_01\" id=\"tag_17_44_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "bind — bind a name to a socket",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_02\" id=\"tag_17_44_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_socket.h.html\">sys/socket.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint bind(int</tt> <i>socket</i><tt>, const struct sockaddr *</tt><i>address</i><tt>,<br>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; socklen_t</tt> <i>address_len</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_03\" id=\"tag_17_44_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]bind[/I5]() function shall assign a local socket address [I6]address[/I6] to a socket identified by descriptor [I7]socket[/I7]\nthat has no local socket address assigned. Sockets created with the [A8][I9]socket[/I9]()[/A8] function\nare initially unnamed; they are identified only by their address family.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A8": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/socket.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I10]bind[/I10]() function takes the following arguments:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00008",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[I11]socket[/I11]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00009",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Specifies the file descriptor of the socket to be bound.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00010",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[I12]address[/I12]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00011",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Points to a [B13]sockaddr[/B13] structure containing the address to be bound to the socket. The length and format of the address\ndepend on the address family of the socket.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B13": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00012",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[I14]address_len[/I14]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00013",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     5,
     13
    ],
    "text": "Specifies the length of the [B15]sockaddr[/B15] structure pointed to by the [I16]address[/I16] argument.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B15": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The socket specified by [I17]socket[/I17] may require the process to have appropriate privileges to use the [I18]bind[/I18]()\nfunction.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00015",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "If the address family of the socket is AF_UNIX, the application shall ensure that a null terminator after the pathname is\nincluded in the [I19]sun_path[/I19] member of [I20]address[/I20] as a [B21]sockaddr_un[/B21] structure, and that [I22]address_len[/I22] is at least\n[CODE23] plus the length of the pathname. If the pathname in the [I24]sun_path[/I24] member\nof [I25]address[/I25] names an existing file, including a symbolic link, [I26]bind[/I26]() shall treat the address as already in use; see\nERRORS below.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "B21": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I22": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE23": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>offsetof(struct sockaddr_un, sun_path) + 1</tt>"
     },
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "If the socket address cannot be assigned immediately and O_NONBLOCK is set for the file descriptor for the socket, [I27]bind[/I27]()\nshall fail and set [I28]errno[/I28] to [EINPROGRESS], but the assignment request shall not be aborted, and the assignment shall be\ncompleted asynchronously. Subsequent calls to [I29]bind[/I29]() for the same socket, before the assignment is completed, shall fail and\nset [I30]errno[/I30] to [EALREADY].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I28": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I30": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00017",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "When the assignment has been performed asynchronously, [A31][I32]pselect[/I32]()[/A31], [A33][I34]select[/I34]()[/A33], [A35][I36]poll[/I36]()[/A35], and [A37][I38]ppoll[/I38]()[/A37] shall indicate that the file descriptor for the socket is ready for reading and\nwriting.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A31": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pselect.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A33": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/select.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A35": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/poll.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A37": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/ppoll.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00018",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A39][/A39]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A39": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_04\" id=\"tag_17_44_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00019",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I40]bind[/I40]() shall return 0; otherwise, -1 shall be returned and [I41]errno[/I41] set to indicate the\nerror.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00020",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A42][/A42]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A42": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_05\" id=\"tag_17_44_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I43]bind[/I43]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I43": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00022",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EADDRINUSE]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00023",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The specified address is already in use.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00024",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EADDRNOTAVAIL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00025",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The specified address is not available from the local machine.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00026",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[EAFNOSUPPORT]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00027",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The specified address is not a valid address for the address family of the specified socket.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00028",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[EALREADY]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00029",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "An assignment request is already in progress for the specified socket.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00030",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[EBADF]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00031",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     21
    ],
    "text": "The [I44]socket[/I44] argument is not a valid file descriptor.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I44": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00032",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[EINPROGRESS]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00033",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     25
    ],
    "text": "O_NONBLOCK is set for the file descriptor for the socket and the assignment cannot be immediately performed; the assignment\nshall be performed asynchronously.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00034",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00035",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     29
    ],
    "text": "The socket is already bound to an address, and the protocol does not support binding to a new address; or the socket has been\nshut down.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00036",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     31
    ],
    "text": "[ENOBUFS]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00037",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     33
    ],
    "text": "Insufficient resources were available to complete the call.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00038",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[ENOTSOCK]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00039",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     37
    ],
    "text": "The [I45]socket[/I45] argument does not refer to a socket.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I45": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00040",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[EOPNOTSUPP]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00041",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     3,
     41
    ],
    "text": "The socket type of the specified socket does not support binding to an address.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00042",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     5
    ],
    "text": "If the address family of the socket is AF_UNIX, then [I46]bind[/I46]() shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I46": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00043",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EACCES]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00044",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     5
    ],
    "text": "A component of the path prefix denies search permission, or the requested name requires writing in a directory with a mode that\ndenies write permission.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00045",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EDESTADDRREQ] or [EISDIR]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00046",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I47]address[/I47] argument is a null pointer.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00047",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[EILSEQ]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00048",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The last pathname component is not a portable filename, and cannot be created in the target directory.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00049",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[EIO]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00050",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     17
    ],
    "text": "An I/O error occurred.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00051",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[ELOOP]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00052",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     21
    ],
    "text": "A loop exists in symbolic links encountered during resolution of the pathname in [I48]address[/I48].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I48": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00053",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[ENAMETOOLONG]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00054",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     25
    ],
    "text": "The length of a component of a pathname is longer than {NAME_MAX}.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00055",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[ENOENT]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00056",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     29
    ],
    "text": "A component of the path prefix of the pathname in [I49]address[/I49] does not name an existing file or the pathname is an empty\nstring.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00057",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     31
    ],
    "text": "[ENOENT] or [ENOTDIR]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00058",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     33
    ],
    "text": "The pathname in [I50]address[/I50] contains at least one non-&lt;slash&gt; character and ends with one or more trailing &lt;slash&gt;\ncharacters. If the pathname without the trailing &lt;slash&gt; characters would name an existing file, an [ENOENT] error shall not\noccur.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I50": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00059",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[ENOTDIR]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00060",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     37
    ],
    "text": "A component of the path prefix of the pathname in [I51]address[/I51] names an existing file that is neither a directory nor a\nsymbolic link to a directory, or the pathname in [I52]address[/I52] contains at least one non-&lt;slash&gt; character and ends with one\nor more trailing &lt;slash&gt; characters and the last pathname component names an existing file that is neither a directory nor a\nsymbolic link to a directory.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I51": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00061",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[EROFS]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00062",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     7,
     41
    ],
    "text": "The name would reside on a read-only file system.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00063",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I53]bind[/I53]() function may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I53": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00064",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EACCES]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00065",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The specified address is protected and the current user does not have permission to bind to it.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00066",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00067",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I54]address_len[/I54] argument is not a valid length for the address family.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00068",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[EISCONN]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00069",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The socket is already connected.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00070",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[ELOOP]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00071",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     17
    ],
    "text": "More than {SYMLOOP_MAX} symbolic links were encountered during resolution of the pathname in [I55]address[/I55].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00072",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[ENAMETOOLONG]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00073",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     29,
     11,
     21
    ],
    "text": "The length of a pathname exceeds {PATH_MAX}, or pathname resolution of a symbolic link produced an intermediate result with a\nlength that exceeds {PATH_MAX}.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00074",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A56][/A56]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A56": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_06\" id=\"tag_17_44_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00075",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The following code segment shows how to create a socket and bind it to a name in the AF_UNIX domain.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00076",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A57][/A57]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A57": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_07\" id=\"tag_17_44_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00077",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "An application program can retrieve the assigned socket name with the [A58][I59]getsockname[/I59]()[/A58] function.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A58": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/getsockname.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I59": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00078",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "For AF_UNIX sockets, some implementations support an extension where [I60]address_len[/I60] does not have to include a null\nterminator for the pathname stored in [I61]sun_path[/I61], which in turn allows a pathname to be one byte longer. However, such usage\nis not portable, and carries a risk of accessing beyond the intended bounds of the pathname length.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I60": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I61": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00079",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A62][/A62]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A62": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_44_08\" id=\"tag_17_44_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00080",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Implementations are encouraged to have [I63]bind[/I63]() report an [EILSEQ] error if the last component of the address to be bound\nto an AF_UNIX family socket contains any bytes that have the encoded value of a &lt;newline&gt; character.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I63": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
